;--------------------------------------------------------------------
; Self Updater
;--------------------------------------------------------------------
ButtonUpdateMacroSuite:
DriveGet, status, Status, I:\
	if (status = "Ready") {
	Goto, StartPatch
}
Goto, CantPatch
Return


StartPatch:
MsgBox, Now patching the Macro Suite. This may take a moment.`n`nThis suite will restart itself once completed.
PatchDirectory = I:\CS\Prod\Promotions Files\Production Team Files\Production Macros\Install Data ; Network location to retrieve updates from.
MsgBox, The Production Macros will be updated. Retrieving content from:`n%PatchDirectory%
FileCopy, %PatchDirectory%\Changelog.txt, %A_WorkingDir%, 1
FileCopy, %PatchDirectory%\MacroSuite.ahk, %A_WorkingDir%, 1
FileCopy, %PatchDirectory%\Plugin.core, %A_WorkingDir%, 1
FileCopy, %PatchDirectory%\System.core, %A_WorkingDir%, 1
FileCopy, %PatchDirectory%\Plugins\*.plugin, %A_WorkingDir%\Plugins, 1
MsgBox, The update should now be complete. The macros will now reload.
Reload
Return

CantPatch:
MsgBox, Unable to patch. The I:\ drive can not be accessed.`nTry patching again once you have navigated to the I:\ drive manually.
Return

UpdateNotification:
Gui, Hide
MsgBox, Restarting Multi-Tool`n`nThis will retrieve all network resources and send them to memory.`n`nThis fixes blank test member imports.`n`nThis will also apply any updates.
Reload
Return